	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Fuzzy keyword search over a plain-text database you own.

db &lt;words&gt;      search; words match keywords and title words in any order,
                as whole words, prefixes, substrings or in-word letters (stg → staging)
                ↩ copy  ⇧↩ paste  ⌘↩ edit line  ⌥↩ delete  ⌃ show keywords  ⌘L large type
db+ &lt;entry&gt;     add "keywords | title | payload" (title and payload optional)
dbedit          open the database in your editor

Variables: db_file (database path), editor (command template with {file} and {line}),
max_results, python (interpreter, 3.9+).
</string>
